            B.q("sa-m3-4", "sa-monitoring", "Security logs must stay searchable in the workspace for 90 days, then be kept cheaply for seven years and brought back for an occasional investigation. What do you recommend?", listOf("Set interactive retention to 90 days and total retention to seven years, then use search jobs or restore", "Set interactive retention to seven years so analysts can query any record directly in the workspace", "Set workspace retention to 90 days and rely on the Azure activity log for anything older than that", "Export the tables nightly to a data disk on a VM and keep that disk for seven years for investigations"), setOf(0), "A Log Analytics table has interactive retention, when data can be queried normally, and total retention up to 12 years. Between the two the data is kept at low cost, and a search job or restore brings back what an investigation needs.",
                scenario = "Bellwether Insurance keeps sign-in and audit logs for its Android claims app. The regulator requires seven years; analysts query only the last three months day to day.",
                whyWrong = mapOf(
