            B.q("sa-m3-7", "sa-identity", "Conditional Access must require MFA for everyone, but if MFA or the federation service breaks, administrators must still be able to get in. What do you recommend?", listOf("Exclude the Global Administrator role from every Conditional Access policy, so admins keep a way in", "Two cloud-only emergency access accounts, excluded from the policies and monitored", "Two admin accounts synchronised from on-premises AD, excluded from the policies and monitored", "Register a backup SMS number as a second MFA method on every administrator account"), setOf(1), "Emergency access (break-glass) accounts are a small number of cloud-only accounts kept for when normal sign-in fails. They are excluded from policies that could lock everyone out, protected with strong credentials, and alerts fire whenever they are used.",
