            B.q("sa-m3-14", "sa-governance", "The security team must check settings inside the operating systems of Azure and on-premises servers, such as whether TLS 1.0 is disabled, and report compliance centrally. What do you recommend?", listOf("Azure Policy machine configuration on every server, with Azure Arc for the on-premises ones", "Standard Azure Policy definitions auditing the VMs' resource properties at the management group", "Network security groups that block the TLS 1.0 port on every server's subnet", "The Azure activity log sent to Log Analytics, with alerts on configuration changes"), setOf(0), "Azure Policy's machine configuration, formerly guest configuration, checks settings inside a machine's operating system and reports them with the rest of policy compliance. Azure Arc brings on-premises servers under the same policies.",
                scenario = "Granby Bank's API servers for its Android banking app run partly in Azure and partly on-premises. Auditors want proof that old TLS versions are switched off on every server.",
