            B.q("sa-m3-15", "sa-governance", "Every new product team must get the same set of resource groups, networks, policies and role assignments, versioned, and the set must be protected from accidental changes. Blueprints were used before. What do you recommend?", listOf("Keep using Azure Blueprints, with blueprint resource locking set to Read Only", "Bicep modules in a Git repository, deployed by each team as a standard deployment", "Template specs for the versioned templates, deployed as deployment stacks with deny settings", "A management group per team, with Azure Policy initiatives and inherited role assignments"), setOf(2), "Azure Blueprints retires on 31 January 2027. Template specs store versioned Bicep or ARM templates in Azure, and deploying them as deployment stacks keeps the resources managed together, with deny settings that block unwanted changes.",
                scenario = "Copperfield Retail creates a new environment each time it starts a product, such as its latest Android loyalty app. Its platform team built the pattern in Blueprints years ago.",
                whyWrong = mapOf(
