            B.q("sa-m3-20", "sa-relational", "A MySQL-based catalogue gets ten reads for every write, and reads are slowing down. How do you scale reads on Azure Database for MySQL flexible server with the least change?", listOf("Scale the server up to a larger compute size in the same tier", "Add read replicas and send read-only queries to them", "Turn on high availability and send reads to the standby server", "Shard the catalogue across several servers by product range"), setOf(1), "Read replicas are copies kept in sync from the primary. Sending read-only queries to them spreads the read load, while writes stay on the primary.",
